  "issue_date": "2024-05-17",
  "report_week": "20",
  "report_period": "Week 20 (10th May to 17th May 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Greek owners have committed their Capesize \"Corinthian Phoenix\" 179/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) to clients of Hayfin Capital Management at USD 29 mill. Remind you that back in January, the sister vessel \"Athenian Phoenix\" 179/2009 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 23,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Valiant Summer\" 81/2016 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 06/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to clients of Blumenthal at USD 32,5 mill. Note that the same buyers acquired the one-year-younger sister vessel \"The Prosperity\" 81/2017 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 01/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) back in February at USD 31,5 mill. Dongguan Yinghao Shipping committed their Panamax \"Ying Hao 03\" 76/2012 Hudong-Zhonghua, China (SS/DD 05/2027, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at low USD 17 mill. Note that the \"Ying Hao 02\" 75/2012 Guangzhou, China (SS 06/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold in March at USD 16,8 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Delta Avon\" 56/2012 Cosco, China (SS 03/2027, DD 03/2026, BWTS fitted) was committed to Chinese interests at USD 14,3 mill. For comparison, the \"Hony World\" 56/2012 Xiamen, China (SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at USD 14,7 mill. Furthermore, the \"Super Bergkamp\" 55/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2027, DD 04/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed to Greek interests at USD 15,5 mill. Remind you that back in February, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Konrad Schulte\" 55/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at low USD 16 mill.",
    "tankers": "Sanmar Shipping committed their LR2 \"Sanmar Sangeet\" 106/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) at high USD 26 mill. For reference, the Aframax \"Sea Hazel\" 106/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2029, DD 01/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at USD 29 mill. The MR2 \"Pacific Diamond\" 47/2010 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed at mid-high USD 26 mill. Remind you that back in March, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Pacific Jewel\" 48/2009 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 23,7 mill. In addition, Gulf Energy Maritime committed their \"Gulf Esprit\" 46/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 11/2026, BWTS fitted) at USD 22 mill. For comparison, the \"Grance Ace5\" 46/2006 Stx, Korea (SS 04/2026, DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 21 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 15,000/17,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 24,000/26,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 18,000/20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 800K/1M. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 19,600 pd for 3/5 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 19,500 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A generally quiet week for this segment. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/20,000 pd. South East Asian trips into India were fixed around usd 20,000/23,000 pd. South African trips into China were reported at the level of usd 22,000/25,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 220K/250K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A number of West African trips into East Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 6,000/7,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 16,000/17,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast Central America were reported at the level of usd 22,000/24,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
